{"title":"Wisconsin MathCounts","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Wisconsin_MATHCOUNTS\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Wisconsin MATHCOUNTS</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Chapter_Round\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Chapter Round</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#State_Round\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">State Round</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#National_Performance\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">National Performance</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#National_Team\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">National Team</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#AoPS_alum_of_wisconsin_nationals\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">AoPS alum of wisconsin nationals</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Wisconsin_MATHCOUNTS\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"//www.wspe.org/mathcounts/\">Wisconsin MATHCOUNTS</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Wisconsin_MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Wisconsin MATHCOUNTS\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Chapter_Round\">Chapter Round</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Wisconsin_MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Chapter Round\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In Wisconsin, there are a total of 8 chapters. Each sends 2 teams to the state competition.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"State_Round\">State Round</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Wisconsin_MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: State Round\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Countdown Round is official at the state competition. 10th and 9th place compete, and the winner plays 8th, then 7th, and so on. Therefore, the top 3 individuals' spot for Nationals are secured but the places (1st, 2nd, 3rd . . .) are not announced until each person comes up and competes. Therefore, it is very brutal because no one knows how well someone did until the Countdown progresses.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"National_Performance\">National Performance</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Wisconsin_MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: National Performance\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Wisconsin MATHCOUNTS has won the national competition as a team once, in 1998.\nIndividually, Wisconsin has had 2 national winners.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"National_Team\">National Team</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Wisconsin_MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: National Team\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>2019: @JAKEMATH007, @mathpluspianoequalslife, ----, @WIStanford2004\n</p><p>2025: ----, @mithu542, @FJH07, ----\n</p><p>2026: @kingarthur4812, @mithu542, @FJH07, @thisguylool\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"AoPS_alum_of_wisconsin_nationals\">AoPS alum of wisconsin nationals</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Wisconsin_MathCounts&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: AoPS alum of wisconsin nationals\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018114001\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.007 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.008 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 17/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:35471:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018114001 and revision id 283241. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}